    "detailed_description": "<h1>Just Updated</h1><p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game features many improvements, including better graphics, better controls and many new maps, such as the first version of Byilhan's Hotel, an abandoned hospital, the Backrooms and a museum. You can now select the difficulty you want, so that anomalies can be more or less difficult depending on your choice.</p></p><br><h1>About the Game</h1><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >&quot;Exit16: Byilhan Hotel&quot; is a &quot;walking simulator&quot; &amp; &quot;Spot the Difference&quot; game. The game challenges players to unravel hidden anomalies strewn across the enigmatic corridor of the Byilhan Hotel.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Each floor of the hotel presents a unique canvas, with some adorned by the peculiarities of anomalies while others maintain an eerie semblance of normalcy. Your task is to discern the subtle nuances that distinguish the ordinary from the extraordinary, as every object, every angle, and every shadow holds a potential clue.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Traverse the hallways with caution, for not all anomalies reveal themselves readily.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you suspect there is an anomaly, turn back. If you believe everything is normal, that there are no anomalies, do not turn back and continue down the corridor. If you make a mistake, you will know by looking at the level number. If the number has increased, you have made the correct choice. If you return to level 1, you have made a mistake and will need to start over (the anomalies will be different). The goal is to reach the final level.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Navigate the twists and turns of the Byilhan Hotel, unraveling its mysteries one anomaly at a time.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Key Features:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Repeating Hotel Corridor: Explore a hauntingly repetitive environment, where each step could lead to discovery or deception.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >duration: The final version of the game should be about 30 minutes to 1h30</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >&quot;Exit16: Byilhan Hotel&quot; is a &quot;walking simulator&quot; &amp; &quot;Spot the Difference&quot; game. The game challenges players to unravel hidden anomalies strewn across the enigmatic corridor of the Byilhan Hotel.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Each floor of the hotel presents a unique canvas, with some adorned by the peculiarities of anomalies while others maintain an eerie semblance of normalcy. Your task is to discern the subtle nuances that distinguish the ordinary from the extraordinary, as every object, every angle, and every shadow holds a potential clue.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Traverse the hallways with caution, for not all anomalies reveal themselves readily.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you suspect there is an anomaly, turn back. If you believe everything is normal, that there are no anomalies, do not turn back and continue down the corridor. If you make a mistake, you will know by looking at the level number. If the number has increased, you have made the correct choice. If you return to level 1, you have made a mistake and will need to start over (the anomalies will be different). The goal is to reach the final level.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Navigate the twists and turns of the Byilhan Hotel, unraveling its mysteries one anomaly at a time.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Key Features:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Repeating Hotel Corridor: Explore a hauntingly repetitive environment, where each step could lead to discovery or deception.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >duration: The final version of the game should be about 30 minutes to 1h30</p>",
    "short_description": "You're locked in a corridor full of anomalies. You must find all the anomalies in each level to escape.",
